      "message": "Running the added subgroups E2E test on trybots, I found that on `android-dawn-arm-rel` trybot (Backend device `Vulkan_Adreno__TM__640` on Android device Pixel 4), **using `subgroupBroadcast` with `i32` and `u32` types in a workgroup of size 1 will result in Vulkan `CreateComputePipelines` fails** with code VkUnknown. (Please refers to the [testing CL](https://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/196854) and the [corresponding error results](https://ci.chromium.org/ui/p/chromium/builders/try/android-dawn-arm-rel/13225/overview) ) This trybot pass all tests on other workgroup sizes, including 2,3,4, ..., 255, and 256, and using type `f32` can also pass. Other trybots including `android-dawn-arm64-rel` can pass all tests. I thought this might be an device-specific issue, and I am going to file a bug about this.\n\nFor current CL, what shall we do to make progress? Is it sufficient to just suppress this exact case (Type `i32`/`u32`, workgroup size `1`) on ARM and get the CL land?",
